From f02d92d11d426b53b69a63c425de85390ba8ea71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g00rek <76205606+g00rek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:11:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Homa Lawn: Local network, the permission Android 17 needs for
 the link (patch 0037)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Homa Lawn targets SDK 37, so on Android 17 every local-network packet of the app is blocked
without the runtime permission ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK (group Nearby devices): the computer's TLS
handshake on port 47100 never completes and NsdManager.registerService throws
"Missing local network permission". The manifest now declares it, and it is a needed permission:
Settings › Permissions › Local network (allowed before Android 17; the tap shows Android's prompt
through LocalNetworkActivity, or App info when Android no longer shows it), launcher.ping's
permissions.local_network, the Setup reminders notification (Allow local network). It is asked
for once per install with the home screen's first prompt (in the same request as notifications),
and Pair a computer asks for it and says so on the waiting screen while it is missing. Once it is
granted while the process runs, the mDNS advert refused at the link's start is registered
(Nsd.retry, from the prompt's result, every Setup reminders check and the Permissions screen's
resume). The constants are spelled out: Launcher3's framework-16.jar comes first on the compile
classpath and lacks ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK and CINNAMON_BUN.
